{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — is it to maximize total profit (unit price minus raw material cost minus the equipment operating costs), or to maximize total revenue, or to minimize total cost?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The \"Operating Costs at Full Capacity\" column — is this a fixed cost that is incurred whenever the machine is used at all (regardless of how much), or is it a cost that scales proportionally with the fraction of machine hours actually used?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the cost structure (fixed vs. proportional), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a demand limit (maximum number of units that can be sold) for each product, or can the factory sell any quantity it produces?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether demand is capped or unlimited."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the demand limits are not yet confirmed, should I model the plan assuming there is no upper bound on how many units of each product can be sold (i.e., production is limited only by machine hours), or would you prefer I hold that slot open and you confirm the demand caps before I finalize?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding how to handle unconfirmed demand limits (model with no upper bound vs. wait for confirmation), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

